@issue-328 @execute @controller-lease
Feature: Recover only confirmed stale controller leases
  As a developer operating an Oh My Pi / Herdr delivery controller
  I want an explicit recovery option for a confirmed-dead controller lease
  So that a run can resume without weakening live ownership protection

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Reclaim a confirmed-dead lease for the same run
    Given the current checkpoint and controller lease identify the same run
    And the lease's recorded PID is demonstrably absent
    And a successful Herdr agent listing proves the exact recorded controller pane is absent
    When the developer runs "/sdlc-execute --recover-stale" for the current issue selection
    Then the stale lease is reclaimed
    And execute continues through normal controller startup
    And recovery reports "Recovered stale controller lease."

  @SCN002
  Scenario Outline: Preserve live, unknown, malformed, and foreign leases
    Given a controller lease has "<condition>"
    When the developer runs "/sdlc-execute --recover-stale"
    Then execute fails with "controller_lease_held"
    And the lease bytes remain unchanged
    And no worker pane, checkpoint, handoff, branch, verification, or delivery mutation is started

    Examples:
      | condition |
      | a live PID |
      | an unknown PID or pane result |
      | a malformed or unreadable record |
      | a foreign run identity |

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Protect a changed or newly-created lease atomically
    Given a same-run lease was confirmed to have an absent owner from an earlier observation
    When the lease changes or a new lease appears before stale recovery completes
    Then recovery fails with "controller_lease_held"
    And it does not delete, overwrite, or restore over the changed or newly-created lease
    And the latest lease bytes remain intact

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Preserve default and retained-worker behavior
    Given an existing lease or an execute lifecycle that uses owned workers
    When execute runs without "--recover-stale", or with the existing "--retain-worker" option
    Then ordinary existing-lease rejection and controller/worker ownership behavior remain unchanged
    And stale-owner inspection and reclamation occur only when "--recover-stale" is explicitly supplied
    And "--retain-worker" continues to control intentional worker retention independently
